WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.784
Emperor Taiwu of Northern Wei unified the north and became a very powerful emperor.

00:00:06.134 --> 00:00:10.694
He inspected the lands of the north, his armies mighty and well-ordered.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:16.516
At that time Buddhism flourished in the north: there were many temples, and many people believed in the Buddha.

00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:24.570
In the year 446, Emperor Taiwu, for political and religious reasons, ordered a crackdown on Buddhism.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:30.344
Many temples were torn down and the Buddhist scriptures were taken away — a scene that grieved the heart.

00:00:30.694 --> 00:00:35.638
Watching the fallen temples, the monks could not hold back their tears.

00:00:35.988 --> 00:00:43.068
The monks were forced to return to secular life, taking off their robes and once again living as ordinary commoners.

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:47.666
They returned to their home villages to farm, slowly adapting to their new lives.

00:00:48.016 --> 00:00:56.680
This is one of the famous suppression-of-Buddhism events in history, and it makes people reflect on the complex relationship between religion and politics.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.894
Later emperors changed the policy, and Buddhism gradually recovered.

